"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[978],{2297(e,o,t){t.r(o),t.d(o,{_pageData:()=>n,default:()=>l});var a=t(641);const n=JSON.parse('{"path":"/bagisto-connector/installation.html","title":"Installation & Plugin Updates","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"next":"/bagisto-connector/connection-setup.md"},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"bagisto-connector/installation.md"}'),s={name:"installation.md"},l=(0,t(6262).A)(s,[["render",function(e,o,t,n,s,l){return(0,a.uX)(),(0,a.CE)("div",null,[...o[0]||(o[0]=[(0,a.Fv)('<h1 id="installation-plugin-updates" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#installation-plugin-updates"><span>Installation &amp; Plugin Updates</span></a></h1><p>Learn how to download, install, configure, and safely update the WooCommerce to Bagisto Connector plugin on your WordPress site.</p><hr><h2 id="_1-installation-via-wordpress-dashboard" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-installation-via-wordpress-dashboard"><span>1. Installation via WordPress Dashboard</span></a></h2><p>This is the recommended and easiest installation method:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Download the ZIP File:</strong> Log into your <a href="https://wordpress.org/plugins/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WordPress</a> account and download the <code>bagisto-connector</code> plugin ZIP file.</p></li><li><p><strong>Navigate to Plugins:</strong> Log into your WordPress admin panel and go to <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Add New</strong>. <img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/upload-plugin.png" alt="Navigate to Plugins and Add New"></p></li><li><p><strong>Upload the Plugin:</strong> Click <strong>Upload Plugin</strong> at the top. Choose the downloaded ZIP file and click <strong>Install Now</strong>.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/activate-plugin.png" alt="Choose ZIP File and Activate Plugin"></p></li><li><p><strong>Activate:</strong> Once the upload completes, click <strong>Activate Plugin</strong>.</p></li></ol><hr><h2 id="_2-installation-via-ftp-sftp" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-installation-via-ftp-sftp"><span>2. Installation via FTP / SFTP</span></a></h2><p>If you experience server upload limits, upload the plugin files directly:</p><ol><li><strong>Extract the ZIP File:</strong> Extract the downloaded <code>bagisto-connector.zip</code> on your local computer. This creates a folder named <code>bagisto-connector</code>.</li><li><strong>Connect to your Server:</strong> Use an FTP client (such as FileZilla) to connect to your web host.</li><li><strong>Upload the Folder:</strong> Navigate to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> and upload the extracted folder.</li><li><strong>Activate:</strong> Go to <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Installed Plugins</strong> in your WordPress dashboard, find &quot;WooCommerce to Bagisto Connector&quot;, and click <strong>Activate</strong>.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="_3-module-translation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-module-translation"><span>3. Module Translation</span></a></h2><p>The WooCommerce to Bagisto Connector plugin is localization-ready and can be translated into any language. Follow these steps to translate the interface:</p><ol><li><strong>Locate translation template:</strong> The translation template file (<code>.pot</code>) is located in the plugin&#39;s <code>/languages/</code> directory.</li><li><strong>Use Translation Tool:</strong> Open the <code>.pot</code> template file using a tool like <strong>Poedit</strong> or the <strong>Loco Translate</strong> plugin.</li><li><strong>Translate Strings:</strong> Translate the source strings to your target language.</li><li><strong>Save Files:</strong> Save the translation files with the correct locale extension: <ul><li><code>.po</code> file (e.g., <code>wkwcbagcon-fr_FR.po</code> for French)</li><li><code>.mo</code> compiled translation file (e.g., <code>wkwcbagcon-fr_FR.mo</code>)</li></ul></li><li><strong>Deployment Path:</strong> Upload the saved <code>.po</code> and <code>.mo</code> files to the standard WordPress languages directory:<div class="language-text line-numbers-mode" data-highlighter="prismjs" data-ext="text"><pre><code class="language-text"><span class="line">/wp-content/languages/plugins/</span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><div class="line-numbers" aria-hidden="true" style="counter-reset:line-number 0;"><div class="line-number"></div></div></div>This ensures that translation files are not overwritten when you update the plugin.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="_4-safe-update-procedures" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-safe-update-procedures"><span>4. Safe Update Procedures</span></a></h2><p>Webkul regularly releases updates containing features, bug fixes, and performance improvements. Follow these guidelines to update safely:</p><h3 id="data-safety" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#data-safety"><span>Data Safety</span></a></h3><p>All configurations and logs are stored securely in your website&#39;s database. <strong>Deleting the plugin files will not delete your connection settings or log history.</strong></p><blockquote><p>[!WARNING] Before performing any plugin updates, always take a complete backup of your database.</p></blockquote><h3 id="update-workflow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#update-workflow"><span>Update Workflow:</span></a></h3><ol><li>Go to <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Installed Plugins</strong>.</li><li>Find <strong>WooCommerce to Bagisto Connector</strong> and click <strong>Deactivate</strong>.</li><li>Click <strong>Delete</strong> to remove the old version files (your database data remains safe).</li><li>Upload the new version ZIP file via <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Add New</strong> &gt; <strong>Upload Plugin</strong>.</li><li>Click <strong>Activate Plugin</strong>. The plugin will automatically run migration checks and apply database updates if required.</li></ol>',22)])])}]])}}]);